{
  "functions": [
    "MakemkvTool.scanDrives",
    "MakemkvTool.listing",
    "MakemkvTool.rip",
    "MakemkvTool.backup"
  ],
  "description": "MakemkvTool against a scripted launcher (plan §26, 'Adapters'), the same on the three platforms. The launcher emits given.transcript (a file in shared/fixtures) or given.lines, one line at a time, as stdout; when the tool stops it, no more lines come and the process ends with status -1, signal 15 (cancelled when the reason was cancelled); otherwise it ends with given.exitCode, after creating the files given.writes in the destination (a name with / makes its folders; \"\" makes the destination itself a file). given.transcriptFails makes the process report process.noTranscript (expect.transcriptProblem is the run's). given.cancelAfterLines cancels the call's token after that many lines; given.deleteDestinationAfterLines deletes the destination folder (and what is in it) after that many lines. The isolation is a fake that records prepare / firstOutput / release and gives HOME = <work> (<root>/home) and, with given.profileXml, the profile <work>/profile.mmcp.xml. The locator finds makemkvcon at /opt/makemkvcon unless given.makemkvcon is null. Paths: <root> is an empty temporary folder; given.destination and given.existing are relative to it. The destination folder is created first unless given.destinationExists is false (a backup's must not exist: makemkvcon refuses one that does, so those cases set it false). The run's produced files are the names new in the destination that RunOutcome.products counts (for a backup that came out as one file at the destination, product image: that file, whatever its name); a destination that can't be listed fails the call. expect.arguments, environment, workingDirectory, stopPolicy, stallTimeout and transcriptFile are those of the ProcessSpec; status is RunOutcome's (success, errors, failed, cancelled); errorContains is part of its error rendered in English; errorCode its code; produced the outcome's produced names; error is the code of the failure thrown before anything runs; stopped says whether the tool stopped the process, stopReason why (policy for MakeMKV's space warning and a renumbered drive, cancelled for the caller's token); linesRead how many lines it had read by then.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "scan-drives",
      "from": [
        "rearchitecture-plan §10.1 scanDrives (info disc:9999)"
      ],
      "given": {
        "call": "scanDrives",
        "transcript": "drive-scan.txt",
        "exitCode": 0
      },
      "expect": {
        "arguments": [
          "-r",
          "--cache=1",
          "info",
          "disc:9999"
        ],
        "environment": {},
        "workingDirectory": null,
        "lease": [],
        "drives": [
          [
            0,
            "inserted",
            "/dev/rdisk4"
          ],
          [
            1,
            "emptyClosed",
            "/dev/rdisk5"
          ],
          [
            2,
            "emptyOpen",
            "/dev/rdisk6"
          ],
          [
            3,
            "loading",
            "/dev/rdisk7"
          ],
          [
            4,
            "inserted",
            "/dev/rdisk8"
          ],
          [
            5,
            "noDrive",
            ""
          ],
          [
            6,
            "noDrive",
            ""
          ],
          [
            7,
            "noDrive",
            ""
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "listing",
      "from": [
        "rearchitecture-plan §10.1 listing (info)"
      ],
      "given": {
        "call": "listing",
        "source": {
          "iso": "/discs/Movie.iso"
        },
        "options": {
          "minLengthSeconds": 120
        },
        "profileXml": "<profile/>",
        "transcript": "info-dvd.txt",
        "exitCode": 0
      },
      "expect": {
        "arguments": [
          "-r",
          "--progress=-same",
          "--messages=-stdout",
          "--noscan",
          "--profile=<work>/profile.mmcp.xml",
          "--minlength=120",
          "info",
          "iso:/discs/Movie.iso"
        ],
        "environment": {
          "HOME": "<work>"
        },
        "workingDirectory": "<work>",
        "stopPolicy": "terminateFirst",
        "lease": [
          "prepare",
          "firstOutput",
          "release"
        ],
        "listing": {
          "volumeName": "One_Piece_S3_P1_D1",
          "titles": 3
        },
        "status": "success",
        "version": "MakeMKV v2.0.0 darwin(arm64-release)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rip-mkv-rip",
      "from": [
        "shared/fixtures/rip-outcomes.json"
      ],
      "given": {
        "call": "rip",
        "source": {
          "drive": {
            "index": 0,
            "device": "/dev/rdisk4"
          }
        },
        "title": "all",
        "destination": "staging",
        "transcript": "mkv-rip.txt",
        "exitCode": 0,
        "writes": [
          "title_t00.mkv"
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "success",
        "errorContains": null,
        "arguments": [
          "-r",
          "--progress=-same",
          "--messages=-stdout",
          "--noscan",
          "mkv",
          "dev:/dev/rdisk4",
          "all",
          "<root>/staging"
        ],
        "lease": [
          "prepare",
          "firstOutput",
          "release"
        ],
        "debugLog": "/Users/user/MakeMKV_log.txt",
        "produced": [
          "title_t00.mkv"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rip-rip-read-errors",
